<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85193" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύ-πλαγκτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάζω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>much-wandering, wide-roving,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληϊστῆρσι π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.425
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				511
			</span></i>; of <i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				572
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἔτεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					1.186
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἂν εἰδείης ἕτερον . .
					πολυπλαγκτότερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>HF</u>
					1197
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>evermoving,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰκτῖνοι</span> (prob.l.) <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				1257
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					16.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>much-erring,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πραπίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1424
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Rome</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>driving far from one's course,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.308
				</span></i>
			 (unless in signf. <i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i>).—In <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				615
			</span></i> (lyr.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἐλπίς</span> may be
			either <i>wandering, uncertain</i> hope, or, <i>misleading,
				deceitful;</i> cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολυπλανής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
